  "routine:main_tab": "ritual",
  "routine:steps": [
    {
      "detail": [
        "No phone. No email. No scrolling. A few deep breaths, gratitude, a prayer, or just sitting.",
        "**Never scales.** One minute in every version. It's the cheapest step and the one that decides whether the rest happens — once you've taken outside input you're not talking to the same nervous system."
      ],
      "id": "int",
      "mins": {
        "floor": 1,
        "full": 1,
        "hour": 1
      },
      "name": "Intention"
    },
    {
      "detail": [
        "Workout, yoga, or a brisk walk. Enough to raise your heart rate, not enough to leave you depleted for the frog.",
        "**The purpose is clearing restlessness, not training stimulus.** That's why it comes first — most people fail at meditation because they sit down still full of energy.",
        "**This is the swing variable.** When the hour becomes fifty minutes, cut here — not the sit. Fifteen minutes does most of what twenty-five does for this purpose. If fitness is a real goal, train it as its own session later in the day."
      ],
      "id": "mov",
      "mins": {
        "floor": 3,
        "full": 30,
        "hour": 25
      },
      "name": "Move"
    },
    {
      "detail": [
        "Optional. Post-workout is the tolerable window — warm core, elevated circulation.",
        "**Skip entirely when sick.** The most skippable step here; treat it as a bonus, never a requirement."
      ],
      "id": "cold",
      "mins": {
        "floor": 0,
        "full": 3,
        "hour": 3
      },
      "name": "Cold"
    },
    {
      "detail": [
        "Rhythmic breathing to settle. In the hour version this is a bridge into the sit rather than a standalone practice — it's what makes the next twelve minutes work.",
        "**Short on time:** half-counts. **Anxious, mind spinning:** take it to ten minutes and borrow them from movement.",
        "On the floor version this replaces meditation entirely — three minutes of sitting is mostly spent settling, but breath acts fast and needs no runway."
      ],
      "id": "brt",
      "mins": {
        "floor": 3,
        "full": 5,
        "hour": 5
      },
      "name": "Breath"
    },
    {
      "detail": [
        "Seated meditation. The first real payoff of the hour.",
        "**Below roughly ten minutes you spend the whole sit settling.** Past it, you get actual sitting — which is why this doesn't appear in the floor version at all.",
        "Don't shorten this to protect the workout. It's the reason you're running the hour rather than the ten."
      ],
      "id": "sit",
      "mins": {
        "floor": 0,
        "full": 20,
        "hour": 12
      },
      "name": "Sit"
    },
    {
      "detail": [
        "Brain dump whatever's loud, then plan the day.",
        "**Eight minutes is the threshold.** Enough to surface something and resolve it — at three you either write nothing, or open something you can't close.",
        "Self-awareness is still elevated from the sit. That's what you're spending here."
      ],
      "id": "pag",
      "mins": {
        "floor": 0,
        "full": 12,
        "hour": 8
      },
      "name": "Page"
    },
    {
      "detail": [
        "**Eye contact, steady breathing, one minute.** Then one honest sentence out loud about your current state. Not a fix — true. \"I'm tired and a little scared about today.\"",
        "**Then immediately:** \"And I'm not leaving. I'm here with you.\" You're proving the promise before you ask yourself to believe anything. Skipping this is what makes affirmations feel like lying to your face.",
        "**The five, three times each.** Flat, then louder, then like you're telling someone who doubted you. Pause between them and let the meaning land in your body before moving on.",
        "**Then the three present-tense lines** about today specifically. Hands over your heart or your face — anchoring the state to touch means you can recall it later by repeating the gesture.",
        "**Close quietly:** \"I'm proud of you. Let's go.\" Then walk away. Don't linger and undo it by drifting back into inspecting your face."
      ],
      "id": "mir",
      "mins": {
        "floor": 3,
        "full": 5,
        "hour": 5
      },
      "name": "Mirror"
    }
  ],
